Note: no issues if I remove `@psalm-template` from `makeConcrete()` and hardcode the generic type:

```php
<?php

/** @psalm-template SomeType */
interface ParentType
{
    /** @psalm-return SomeType */
    function foo();
}

/** @psalm-template SomeOtherType */
interface ChildType extends ParentType
{
}

class ConcreteParameter
{
    function sayHello() : string
    {
        return 'hi';
    }
}

/**
 * @psalm-return ConcreteParameter&ChildType<ConcreteParameter>&ParentType<ConcreteParameter>
 */
function makeConcrete() : object
{
    return new class() extends ConcreteParameter implements ChildType {
        public function foo() {
            return $this;
        }
    };
}

echo makeConcrete()->foo()->sayHello();
```
